            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court held that the phrase \u201cnotice to appear\u201d in the immigration statute requires a single written notice document, not multiple documents."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "52e1c2d11acf20ed9b9c9c493251eace454892f9c420d41a236199b7ae3d5150",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-52e1c2d11acf-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case turned on how the statutory language affects whether a non\u2011citizen receives proper notice for cancellation\u2011of\u2011removal eligibility."
      }
    ],
