              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The government argues that the statute does not contemplate multiple documents and that requiring a single notice would unfairly limit its ability to provide timely hearing information."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "David Zimmer",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "dd9c73c93a20ee79412ce7b1086ff968685e3e4a30812095f8302ee4e2dd7ea7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-dd9c73c93a20-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Attorney David Zimmer argues that the statutory text and the IIRIRA changes make clear that a \u201cnotice to appear\u201d is a specific document, not an abstract concept."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Government",
      "status": "complete",
