              "ev-52e1c2d11acf-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court\u2019s interpretation determines whether a non\u2011citizen can satisfy the written\u2011notice requirement with a single document or with multiple documents, directly affecting eligibility for cancellation of removal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dd9c73c93a20ee79412ce7b1086ff968685e3e4a30812095f8302ee4e2dd7ea7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd9c73c93a20-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 76,
              "start": 76
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Congressional intent, as reflected in the statutory text, requires written notice to be in writing and served personally or by mail, underscoring the importance of the notice\u2019s form."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "52e1c2d11acf20ed9b9c9c493251eace454892f9c420d41a236199b7ae3d5150",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-52e1c2d11acf-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, the dissent warns that the decision may increase administrative costs and provide little benefit to non\u2011citizens who have already received notice."
      }
    ],
